            "b1ab22575d4d13e50c9477035705bc469d5f629d9c24f93b0df666e1b62de89f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "step_id": 65,
          "canonical_step_sha256": "e3dc395b65ff5689d2cfbbc7fb475f6fe7d492b628b5347eb7edd73618efada8",
          "message": "Let me verify the public API via `go doc`.",
          "tool_calls_sha256": [
            "e004c4bfd853140ead799dd41f72e59cff45f73e0babc843c4a107ada902734c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "step_id": 84,
          "canonical_step_sha256": "5ef5e224dae0f605e00d54027701083ed7f3ab60594d3c0233d9ffdab80d45ea",
          "message": "Let me verify the final branch state and run one last full verification including a fresh build.",
          "tool_calls_sha256": [
            "8e957943c8b8933d01fc0a1af5ce07086a9caeb8406ce59ccd38bcc3ec00a04f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "step_id": 85,
          "canonical_step_sha256": "4277089bd2971d8bb2fc11c456cea6631934c7ad1a6d0accc0e1a252908f1da8",
          "message": "All changes are implemented, committed on the `feature/ansi-truncation` branch, and verified. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**New `ansi` subpackage** (`ansi/ansi.go`):\n- `TokenType` enum (`TokenText`, `TokenSGR`, `TokenReset`, `TokenHyperlinkOpen`, `TokenHyperlinkClose`)\n- `Token` struct with `Type`, `Raw`, `Text`\n- `Tokenize`, `TruncateANSI`, `TruncateOptions`, `StripANSI`, `ANSIWidth`, `HasANSI`\n- CSI/OSC sequences are never split and have zero visible width; Unicode widths (wide runes, U+200B) handled via `uniseg`\n- Preserve-resets re-opens active styles after reset runs; reset detection covers `ESC[m` and any `ESC[...m` with a parameter parsing to 0\n- Tail counts toward width and inherits active style; final SGR reset appended when styles are active; open OSC 8 hyperlinks closed\n\n**termenv-level wrappers** (`ansi.go`): `TruncateANSI`, `TruncateOptions`, `StripANSI`, `ANSIWidth`, `HasANSI`\n\n**Style** (`style.go`): `PreserveResets()`, `Truncate(int, TruncateOptions)`, and `Styled` now re-opens the enclosing style after reset runs when preserve-resets is enabled\n\n**Output** (`output.go`): `WithPreserveResets(bool)`, `String` creating styles that inherit the default, `Truncate` (enables preserve when `outputDefault || opts.PreserveResets`; Ascii returns text with tail and no ANSI)\n\n**Template helpers** (`templatehelper.go`): `Output.TemplateFuncs()` propagates the default to all helpers; added `Truncate(width, tail, string)` and `truncate(width, string)`\n\nAll existing tests pass, and the implementation builds cleanly.",
          "tool_calls_sha256": [
            "f25360b5804bb8bf8a969a255c9c3e7dbd2c22e6b7720a94c60a58522dabeadb"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
