          "canonical_step_sha256": "b71ffd304079dd139f72ca1d7e3df9f1f6b1f8c91e51e5fbef68b3dde5d9d00c",
          "message": "The implementation is complete and committed. Let me provide a final summary and submit.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n- **`event.go`**: Added `BatchDurableInfo` struct, `EventListener.BatchDurable` callback field, default no-op in `EnsureDefaults`, forwarding in `TeeEventListener`, and a non-nil handler in `MakeLoggingEventListener`.\n- **`options.go`**: Added `WriteOptions.CommitCorrelationID` + `GetCommitCorrelationID()`, and private `Options` fields to track whether `BatchDurable` was user-configured (since `EnsureDefaults` installs a no-op).\n- **`wal` / `record`**: Extended `wal.SyncOptions` with `OnSyncComplete`, and plumbed it through both the standalone `LogWriter` sync queue and the failover `recordQueue`, invoking it after the sync error is recorded but before the commit's WaitGroup is signaled.\n- **`batch.go`**: Added durability tracking fields to `Batch` (job ID, seqnum, correlation ID, batch size, key count, apply/sync durations, fired flag), and made `SyncWait` invoke the durable callback.\n- **`commit.go` / `db.go`**: Wired the durability tracker into `commitWrite` (prepares tracking + WAL callback), `commitApply` (apply duration), `Commit`/`directWrite` (fires the event after both apply and sync complete), `Close` (unblocks waiters), and `Metrics()`.\n- **`durability.go`** (new): The `durabilityTracker` and all public DB methods (`WaitForDurability*`, `WaitForJobDurability*`, `DurableState`, `DurabilityNotify`, `DurabilityStats`), with bounded job retention, bounded notify subscriptions, and first-error latching.\n- **`metrics.go`**: Added `DurableCommitCount` and `DurableCommitDuration`, accumulated only when `BatchDurable` is configured.\n- **Tests**: Added `durability_test.go`, commit-pipeline failure tests, and WAL callback tests covering success, error, no-sync-wait, large batches, DisableWAL, DB close, context cancellation, notify bounds, job unknown/expired, metrics, and TeeEventListener.\n\nAll root-package tests, record/wal tests, race tests, invariant tests, and the full module test suite (excluding `internal/lint`, which fails only because it needs network access to download tools) pass.",
          "tool_calls_sha256": [
            "8d29e85ed9e3dd6fd92c3e1ab84098317289e7efa2ad4bc57bfbf288c7a0d0f7"
          ]
        }
